# Database Schema

Cloudflare D1 (SQLite). 11 tables, all with an `environment` column for row-level isolation.

## Entity relationships

```mermaid
erDiagram
    enquiries {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT email
        TEXT name
        TEXT dob
        TEXT age_group_id FK
        TEXT invite_id FK
        INTEGER processed
        TEXT events "JSON array"
        TEXT environment
    }
    invites {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT token
        TEXT enquiry_id FK
        TEXT status "pending|sent|accepted|expired"
        INTEGER send_attempts
    }
    bookings {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT enquiry_id FK
        TEXT age_group_id FK
        TEXT session_date
        TEXT status "confirmed|cancelled|attended|no_show"
        TEXT checked_in_at
    }
    age_groups {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT code
        TEXT booking_type "taster|waitlist"
        INTEGER age_min_aug31
        INTEGER age_max_aug31
        TEXT session_days "JSON"
        INTEGER capacity_per_session
        INTEGER active
    }
    academy_waitlist {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT enquiry_id FK
        TEXT season_id FK
        TEXT token
        TEXT response "yes|no|null"
        INTEGER is_returning
    }
    academy_seasons {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT label
        TEXT status "upcoming|open|closed|archived"
    }
    athletes {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT enquiry_id FK
        TEXT name
        TEXT emergency_contact_name
        TEXT emergency_contact_phone
        TEXT medical_info
        TEXT last_attended_at
        INTEGER flagged_absent
    }
    attendance_log {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT person_id "athlete.id or enquiry.id"
        TEXT person_type "member|taster"
        TEXT person_name "denormalised"
        TEXT session_date
        TEXT marked_by "coach email"
    }

    enquiries ||--o{ invites : has
    enquiries ||--o{ bookings : has
    enquiries ||--o{ academy_waitlist : has
    enquiries ||--o| athletes : becomes
    invites ||--o{ bookings : used-for
    age_groups ||--o{ bookings : categorises
    academy_seasons ||--o{ academy_waitlist : contains
```

## Table reference

| Table | Migration | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `enquiries` | 0001 | Every registration. Central record — event log stored here. |
| `invites` | 0001 | Booking invite tokens. One per enquiry. |
| `age_groups` | 0001 | All age group config — admin editable at runtime. |
| `bookings` | 0001 | Confirmed taster sessions. |
| `academy_seasons` | 0001 | Academy programme seasons. |
| `academy_waitlist` | 0001 | Waitlist entries with response tracking. |
| `email_templates` | 0001 | Editable templates with `{{variable}}` substitution. |
| `membership_otps` | 0001 | One-time tokens for membership form access. |
| `membership_forms` | 0002 | Submitted membership form JSON payloads. |
| `athletes` | 0004 | Active members (created from membership forms). |
| `attendance_log` | 0004 | Immutable safeguarding audit trail. |

## enquiries.events — the event log

```mermaid
timeline
    title Example enquiry event log
    booking_invite_sent  : Enquiry processed
    booking_created      : Parent books session
    reminder_sent        : 7 days before session
    attendance_recorded  : Admin marks attended
    membership_invite_sent : OTP email sent
    membership_form_submitted : Parent completes form
```

Valid event types: `academy_waitlist_added` · `academy_response_received` · `booking_invite_sent` · `booking_created` · `invite_expired` · `invite_resent` · `reminder_sent` · `attendance_recorded` · `membership_invite_sent` · `membership_form_submitted`

## Age groups — runtime configurable

All boundaries stored in D1, editable via Settings. Nothing hardcoded.

| Code | Label | Type | Age on 31 Aug | Sessions | Capacity |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `u11` | U11 Academy | waitlist | 9–10 | Sat + Tue | 40/season |
| `u13` | U13 | taster | 11–12 | Tuesday | 2/session |
| `u15` | U15 and older | taster | 13–120 | Tuesday | 2/session |
| `u17` | U17 | taster | 15–16 | Tuesday | 2/session |
| `u20` | U20 | taster | 17–19 | Tuesday | 2/session |

> UK Athletics is updating age group boundaries. Because they are stored in D1, the admin can update them without a code deployment.

